{# Per-field citation pointer. The full citation rules live in the preamble's <citations> block (cached once);
   each task just names the field to cite in. Call as `{{ cite_in('reasoning') }}` or `{{ cite_in('summary') }}`. #}
{%- macro cite_in(field_name) -%}
Cite key moments inside `{{ field_name }}` as `(t <seconds>)`, following the Citations rules above.
{%- endmacro -%}

{# Session-level notability, asked of every scanner type. Deliberately independent of the scanner's own
   question so a non-event answer can still flag a session worth watching. Calibration lives in the
   preamble's <notability_calibration> block (cached once). Call as `{{ rate_notability() }}`. #}
{%- macro rate_notability() -%}
Separately from your answer above, judge the session itself: in `notability_reason` name the single moment a product team would most want to see (or say plainly that nothing stands out), then set `notability` per the notability calibration rules. Judge what happened to the person, not whether it answers this scanner's question — a session can be worth watching even when your answer above is a non-event, and a routine session stays low even when your answer is a hit.
{%- endmacro -%}
